cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "AgriSight: Explainable Early Crop Stress Detection"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "C"
    given-names: "Shylaja"
  - family-names: "M"
    given-names: "Sunandita"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shylaja-C/agrisight"
abstract: >
  AgriSight is a research prototype for explainable crop-stress classification
  from leaf photos. It trains convolutional neural networks (custom baseline,
  MobileNetV3-Large, EfficientNet-B0) on PlantVillage lab images, evaluates
  generalisation to real field images (PlantDoc), and uses Grad-CAM to
  visualise model attention. The project studies the lab-to-field domain gap
  and whether field-style data augmentation reduces it.
keywords:
  - crop disease
  - plant leaf classification
  - domain adaptation
  - Grad-CAM
  - explainable AI
  - transfer learning
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-20"
